# WEBKIT_TILE_RESET_LOG=4 (diagnostic, default OFF): print every op of each
# whole-tile recording just before it is replayed, and keep the level-3 pixel
# readback to level 3 only (the readback hides the bug).
#
# On the Jolla Phone 2 (Mali-G610) with GPU tile painting, one early-load
# Wikimedia Commons recording (tile y=10240, 94 ops, no image atlases) replays
# as FULLY TRANSPARENT on the GPU in most cold runs -- a persistent black tile
# until a later full repaint -- while CPU painting replays the very same
# recording correctly. Not an allocation race (WEBKIT_TILE_ALLOC_SYNC 6/12 and
# 4/12 vs 6/12) and not an unfinished paint (WPE_GL_FENCE_DISABLED 6/12). This
# names the op the GPU replay mishandles:
#   [tileop] <tileY> <op> <rect> color=AARRGGBB style= blend= shader= cf= mf= if= aa= m=[matrix] depth=N
